1. Pick up the room key card from the reception desk.
2. Place the welcome brochure on the reception counter.
3. Open the housekeeping storage cabinet.
4. Close the guest room door.
5. Move the luggage trolley to the hotel lobby.
6. Pick up the room service tray from the service counter.
7. Place the umbrella stand near the hotel entrance.
8. Turn off the lobby display screen.
9. Pick up the room key card and place it on the reception desk.
10. Open the housekeeping cabinet and retrieve a clean towel.
11. Pick up the luggage and place it on the luggage trolley.
12. Retrieve the room service tray and place it outside Room 205.
13. Open the linen cabinet and collect a bedsheet.
14. Pick up the information brochure and place it at the concierge desk.
15. Retrieve the cleaning supplies and place them on the housekeeping cart.
16. Pick up the laundry basket and place it in the laundry room.
17. Go to Room 204, collect the room service tray, and return it to the kitchen.
18. Navigate to the laundry room, retrieve clean towels, and deliver them to the housekeeping station.
19. Go to the reception desk, collect the guest luggage, and place it near the elevator.
20. Navigate to the kitchen, collect the meal tray, and deliver it to Room 301.
21. Go to the housekeeping storage room, retrieve fresh bedsheets, and place them on the housekeeping cart.
22. Navigate to the concierge desk, retrieve the hotel information brochure, and deliver it to the lobby.
23. Go to the conference hall, collect the projector remote, and place it on the podium.
24. Navigate to the hotel entrance, collect the umbrella stand, and place it beside the reception desk.
25. Go to the lobby seating area, collect the forgotten backpack, and deliver it to the lost-and-found office.
26. If clean towels are available in the housekeeping station, deliver them to Room 210; otherwise retrieve them from the laundry room.
27. If the room service tray is outside Room 305, return it to the kitchen; otherwise inspect the service counter.
28. If the guest room door is open after checkout, close it before leaving the floor.
29. If luggage is waiting at reception, transport it to the designated guest room; otherwise organize the luggage trolley.
30. If the concierge desk is missing brochures, retrieve additional brochures from storage.
31. If the housekeeping cart is empty, restock it from the linen room.
32. If the conference room is occupied, place the projector remote on the podium; otherwise return it to storage.
33. If the housekeeping storage cabinet is open, close it before returning to the lobby.
34. Carry the glass water jug without spilling it.
35. Transport the guest luggage without dropping or dragging it.
36. Deliver the meal tray while keeping all food containers level.
37. Move the luggage trolley without blocking the hotel corridor.
38. Carry the flower vase carefully without damaging it.
39. Place the clean towels neatly on the housekeeping cart without touching the floor.
40. Transport the projector without disconnecting its power cable.
41. Carry the room key card securely without placing it on the floor.
42. Prepare Room 208 by delivering fresh towels, placing toiletries in the bathroom, arranging the welcome brochure on the table, checking that the room door is closed, and returning to the housekeeping station.
43. Collect all room service trays from the second floor, return them to the kitchen, organize the service counter, and return to the lobby.
44. Restock the housekeeping station by collecting towels, bedsheets, toiletries, and cleaning supplies from storage, placing each item in its designated location, and returning to the linen room.
45. Inspect the hotel lobby, reception, concierge desk, guest corridors, and conference hall for misplaced luggage, unattended items, open storage cabinets, and improperly arranged furniture, correct each issue, and return to reception.
46. Prepare the conference hall by arranging chairs, placing the projector remote on the podium, organizing presentation materials, checking the entrance doors, and returning to the concierge desk.
47. Collect laundry baskets from guest service areas, transport them to the laundry room, organize the housekeeping carts, and return to the housekeeping station.
48. Prepare the hotel for guest check-in by organizing the reception desk, arranging brochures, positioning luggage trolleys, inspecting the lobby seating area, and returning to the entrance.
49. Prepare the hotel for closing operations by collecting room service equipment, organizing housekeeping supplies, securing conference room equipment, ensuring storage cabinets are closed, and returning to reception.
50. Perform a complete hotel facility inspection by checking guest corridors, reception, concierge desk, housekeeping stations, conference hall, restaurant entrance, elevators, and lobby for misplaced items, unattended luggage, open doors, or incomplete room service tasks, resolve each issue, and return to the reception desk.
